From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] hardware_manager: drop container-side suspend hook

Waydroid's IHardware.suspend() Binder callback is invoked by Android's
SystemSuspend HAL once PowerManagerService decides the device should
sleep: typically after Doze has released all wake locks.  Upstream's
default action is to freeze the lxc.payload.<name> cgroup via
`lxc-freeze`, on the assumption that Waydroid is the only suspend
driver on the system.

On WhaleOS this collides with the host's suspend cycle:

  1. host powerd sends SuspendImminent
  2. waydroid_helper's SuspendCoordinator runs `cmd deviceidle force-idle
     deep` to let Android release wake locks early (block_suspend cap
     is required for InputManagerService, so we can't just remove the
     wake-source path).
  3. Android, now in Doze with no wake locks, calls IHardware.suspend()
     -- and the hook freezes lxc.payload.waydroid.
  4. AlarmManager (and other system_server threads) enter
     __refrigerator() mid-epoll_wait.  Any timerfd that fires after
     this point gets EPOLLWAKEUP -> ep_pm_stay_awake() but never
     ep_pm_relax() because ep_send_events() can't run on a frozen
     thread.
  5. The frozen wakeup sources keep the kernel inpr counter > 0
     forever.  When host powerd then reads /sys/power/wakeup_count it
     blocks in pm_get_wakeup_count() (wait_event), wedging the whole
     suspend cycle.  Resume never happens; the device locks up until
     a power button hold.

The host already drives the container correctly via Doze + the
kernel's own freeze_processes() during real suspend, so the
container-side hook is both redundant and harmful.  Make it a no-op.

We deliberately keep this independent of the suspend_action config
key so that no on-device config knob (default "freeze") can re-enable
the broken path.

--- a/tools/services/hardware_manager.py
+++ b/tools/services/hardware_manager.py
@@ -19,11 +19,13 @@ def start(args):
         logging.debug("Function enableBluetooth not implemented")

     def suspend():
-        cfg = tools.config.load(args)
-        if cfg["waydroid"]["suspend_action"] == "stop":
-            tools.actions.session_manager.stop(args)
-        else:
-            tools.actions.container_manager.freeze(args)
+        # WhaleOS: host powerd + waydroid_helper drive container idle
+        # cooperatively via Android Doze (see suspend_coordinator.cc).
+        # Freezing the container here races with the host suspend cycle
+        # and wedges powerd in pm_get_wakeup_count() because the LXC
+        # freezer halts AlarmManager mid-epoll_wait, leaving its
+        # EPOLLWAKEUP wakeup sources active forever.
+        pass

     def reboot():
         helpers.lxc.stop(args)
